  "query_preview": "../Friday through Monday/...\nA ridge of high pressure lasts over the Gulf and panhandle into \nFriday, however a pattern change begins later Friday into the \nweekend with a return of precipitation as a series of systems \nmove into the area. The first front will move in Friday from a low\nin the Bering Sea, pushing into the northern Gulf coast Friday \nnight into Saturday morning, as the strong high pressure still \nlooks to keep the front further westward and not fully pushing \na front into the rest of the panhandle until Saturday night into\nSunday. The timing of this still looks to remain uncertain, \nlargely dependent on how quickly the high pressure begins to break\ndown and allow for the system to push east into the rest of the\npanhandle. Even more of the model guidance tonight is keeping the\nfront further west and only pushing in as far as Yakutat through\nthe start of Saturday, slowing down the onset of precipitation \neven further.\n\nAlongside the remaining uncertainty of timing, the precipitation \ntype expected is still uncertain and will depend on the location,\nas some areas may see cold air damming near the surface Saturday \ninto the overnight hours as the front moves in. With this in \nplace, locations at sea level across the northern panhandle may \ninitially see rain with snow mixing in before the warmer \nsubtropical air fully pushes in and makes its way down from the upper\nlevels to warm the air near the surface enough to transition to \nrain during the day Sunday.\n\nThis more active pattern will continue through the end of the\nweekend and into the start of next week as a series of lows move \ninto the Gulf, keeping wetter and comparatively warmer weather in\nthe forecast compared to this week.",
